    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make recipe a lemon pepper sweet potato crisp. Start by making extra-large breadcrumbs by cutting off the crust of a hunk of bread and slicing it into thin pieces before adding melted butter, salt, cayenne, and grated Parmesan. Add the mixture to a baking sheet and bake it in the oven for around 25 minutes. Sweet potatoes are peeled and cut into similar sizes, and the zest of one lemon is grated over them, along with the juice. Add salt, freshly ground black pepper, cayenne, and melted butter to the mixing bowl and toss everything until it's evenly coated. Once the bread has cooled, add the sweet potato mixture on top and pop it back into the oven for 25 to 30 minutes until the sweet potatoes turn soft and crispy. Whether it's served as a side or as a main course, the crisp has delicious flavor and crunchy texture.",
